# Build context for BOTH images (docker-compose sets `context: .` for api and web,
# and both Dockerfiles run `COPY . .`). Without this file that COPY swept the whole
# working tree into the image: apps/api/.env with the live JWT secrets and database
# password, apps/api/prisma/dev.db (a real SQLite copy of the shop data), and the
# full .git history. Image layers keep whatever they were built with, so deleting a
# file afterwards does not remove it.
#
# Adding a path here is safe only if nothing in either Dockerfile needs it. Both
# install dependencies and compile from source inside the image, so node_modules,
# dist and lockfile-adjacent build output are all rebuilt rather than copied.

# ── secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*

# ── database copies and dumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API talks to Postgres; no database file belongs in the image at all.
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
**/backups
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*

# ── version control and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# ── installed / generated, rebuilt inside the image ────────────────────────
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# ── runtime data that belongs in a volume, not a layer ─────────────────────
apps/api/uploads

# ── noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
